FINDINGS (the measured re-ranking of the strategy's section 3)

1. C1 CONFIRMED AND DOMINANT -- it is not a "15%" item, it is THE item.
   ENERGY2/GPUPOT is replicated O(N^2) and np-INVARIANT (6.0 -> 6.5 s at np8:
   slightly SLOWER from 8-process memory contention). At the sweep cadence
   (only 2 calls!) it is already 31% of the np8 integration wall; at the 4x
   cadence it is 57%. The np8 ADJUST chain (8.9 / 14.8 s) dwarfs every other
   non-scaling phase combined. Post-C1 estimate (slice ~7x + gather ~ P7c):
   asis np8 21.1 -> ~15.5 s, adj4x np8 23.3 -> ~12 s, i.e. phase-sum speedup
   2.9x -> 4.0x (asis) and 2.3x -> 4.5x (adj4x).

2. C2 (regular tail: list post + 2nd FIRR + GPUCOR) DEMOTED. Measured at
   0.27-0.40 s -- the strategy's "force-eval-sized" guess was wrong at this
   N/cadence (the 2nd FIRR covers only regular-block members). Not worth the
   biggest-gather-yet complexity now; re-examine on the GPU build where P7
   collapses and relative weights shift.

3. The decomposed kernels scale essentially perfectly where it matters:
   P7 47.9 -> 6.51 s (7.4x, imbalance < 0.5%). P3 scales 4.7x (latency-bound
   small irregular blocks, plus 0.31 s gather) -- the known copy-algorithm
   small-block limit, not load imbalance.

4. Replicated O(N)/O(NXTLEN) phases (P2 prediction, P4 corrector, P9 SET_JP)
   get 1.5-2x SLOWER at np8 from replicated memory traffic on one node
   (0.63->1.21, 0.49->0.98, 0.03->0.15 s). Still only ~2.3 s combined at np8.
   C3 (corrector fold-in) stays Step-0-gated as planned: P4 = 0.98 s vs the
   existing 0.31 s irregular gather -- decomposing it roughly trades those
   two numbers; marginal until ENERGY2 is gone. C4 (do not decompose
   prediction) is vindicated: P5 = 0.08 s.

5. OUTPUT is 0.9 s/call of file I/O (np-invariant) -- an I/O cost, not a
   compute-decomposition target. Under the production rank-0 guard ranks > 0
   write to /dev/null; per-DELTAT cost is the price of the data product.

6. P6 GPUNB_SEND = 0.03 s on CPU -- confirms it is a non-issue for mpi-cpu
   and remains a flagged mpi-gpu concern only (H->D of all N per regular
   block).

DECISION: implement C1 next (ranged GPUPOT + Allgatherv + replicated
fixed-order summation, the FPOLY0 pattern). Hold C2/C3 until after C1
re-measurement; the GPU build re-runs this matrix before its own ranking.
